_name"}, {"content": "Call to the Boss", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "target date ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a deadline ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know I have a target date coming up for my article.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "business day ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Monday to Friday, 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not sure I can get it done by end of business day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to accommodate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to adapt to a condition ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not sure if we can accommodate a change in schedule.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "publishing house", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a company that publishes books or magazines ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have a deadline at the publishing house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "deliverable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a product that is provided ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have deliverables for the publishing house.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "layout ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way that something is visually organized ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We cannot change the layout at this point.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking for Favors", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " There are different ways to ask for favors. Favors are things we would like other people to do for us. It is best to be as polite as possible when asking for favors.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modals to ask for favors. <br/>For example:<br/>Could/Would you + verb, please?<br/><span class=\"italic\">Could you speak up a little, please? </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use an if-clause. <br/>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I was wondering <span class=\"strong\">if you could</span> give me some ideas to help with the pain.<br/>Would it be okay <span class=\"strong\">if I called</span> tomorrow?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Could you please recommend some alternative therapies? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would it be okay if I used this?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was wondering if you could give me some ideas.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect Continuous vs Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Perfect tenses to talk about an action that is connected to the present in some way.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect Continuous tense</span> to describe: <br/> <ul> \t<li> a single activity that lasts a long time and continues to the present </li><li> an action that is repeated over a long period of time and continues to the present </li><li>when a long activity has just stopped <br> When you use the Present Perfect Continuous tense, you emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">action</span>. <br/><span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I've been making breakfast all morning. (You want to emphasize the action of making breakfast)</li><?ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"underline\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experience. When you use the Present Perfect tense, you emphasize the <span class=\"strong\">result</span> of an action (something you did in the past and now you have an experience from that action). <br/><span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>I've made breakfast. (The action of making breakfast happened, and the result is that breakfast is now ready)</li><?ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've been trying to reach you all day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been running around all day. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've been better. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I've thrown out my back.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I fell down at the bowling alley and haven't been able to walk since. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We've been negotiating with a new publishing house for a different contract.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le03ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine you have to call your boss (or teacher).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of a favor you need to ask them for.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell them what you have been doing lately.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue including all of these things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice your dialogue with your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I use vocabulary about jobs and work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my recent actions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask someone for a favor.", "type": "text"}]}]}